 "result": "{\"answer\": \"35 states. The Equal Rights Amendment, passed by Congress in March 1972, was ratified by 30 states in its first year, but momentum slowed; Indiana became the 35th and final state to ratify before the original deadline, on 18 January 1977. No further states ratified between then and the 22 March 1979 deadline, leaving the total three short of the 38 (three-fourths of the states) needed for adoption. Note that five of those states \u2014 Nebraska, Tennessee, Idaho, Kentucky and South Dakota \u2014 had voted to rescind their ratifications by that point, though the legal validity of such rescissions is disputed. Congress subsequently extended the deadline to 30 June 1982, during which no additional states ratified.\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"abstained\": false}",
